.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 26, 2026
.Dt LOGIN 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm login
.Nd log into the computer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl fp
.Op Fl h Ar hostname
.Op Ar user
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility authenticates a user and starts a session for them on the
current terminal.
.Xr getty 8
runs it once a name has been typed; it is not normally run by hand.
.Pp
Without a
.Ar user ,
.Nm
prompts for one.
Authentication and account checks go through PAM, using the
.Dq login
policy in
.Pa /etc/pam.d/login ;
see
.Xr pam.conf 5 .
After a failed attempt,
.Nm
says
.Dq Login incorrect
and asks again.
Past
.Cm login-backoff
failures it waits five seconds longer before each new attempt, and after
.Cm login-retries
failures it exits.
A login that is not finished within
.Cm login-timeout
seconds is abandoned.
The three values come from the
.Dq default
class in
.Xr login.conf 5 .
.Pp
A user whose password has passed its change time is made to choose a new
one before the session starts.
.Pp
On success,
.Nm
applies the user's login class (resource limits, priority, umask and
environment), changes the terminal's owner to the user, records the
session in
.Pa /var/run/utmpx
and
.Pa /var/log/wtmpx ,
and runs the user's shell as a login shell in the home directory.
Unless the class sets
.Cm hushlogin
or
.Pa ~/.hushlogin
exists, it first prints the message of the day.
.Pp
.Nm
waits for the shell to exit, then closes the PAM session, records the
logout and gives the terminal back to root.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl f
The user has already been authenticated; skip authentication.
.It Fl h Ar hostname
The session comes from
.Ar hostname .
.It Fl p
Keep the environment rather than starting from an empty one.
.El
.Pp
Only the superuser may run
.Nm .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The shell starts with
.Ev HOME ,
.Ev SHELL ,
.Ev USER ,
.Ev LOGNAME ,
.Ev PATH ,
.Ev TERM
and
.Ev MAIL
set, plus whatever the login class and the PAM modules add.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/pam.d/login -compact
.It Pa /etc/login.conf
login classes
.It Pa /etc/motd
message of the day
.It Pa /etc/nologin
refuses logins other than root's while it exists
.It Pa /etc/pam.d/login
the PAM policy
.It Pa /var/run/utmpx
current sessions
.It Pa /var/log/wtmpx
session history
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr utmpx 3 ,
.Xr login.conf 5 ,
.Xr pam.conf 5 ,
.Xr passwd 5 ,
.Xr getty 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
utility appeared in
.At v1 .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD.
